// This project's choices, laid over the machine's ../semel.machine.config by the formula:
// the target and the C standard, spelled out per tool because a tool's settings are
// complete where they are written.
//
// No defines: SQLite's defaults are the build its documentation recommends — threadsafe,
// extension loading on (dlopen is in libSystem), and a shell with no line editing, since
// HAVE_READLINE and HAVE_EDITLINE are unset — so the library and the shell need neither a
// flag nor a library beyond the archive. A define here would be a choice this build exists
// to measure nothing about.
//
// Values are literal: everything after the first `=` is the value, quotes included.

clang.preprocessor.target=arm64-apple-macos14.0
clang.preprocessor.cStandard=c99

clang.compiler.target=arm64-apple-macos14.0
clang.compiler.cStandard=c99
// SQLite's macros expand to comparisons in doubled parentheses, as Lua's do; clang warns
// about each once it reads them preprocessed, where a build from the source sees the
// macros and does not.
clang.compiler.arguments=-Wno-parentheses-equality

clang.linker.target=arm64-apple-macos14.0
